+# Customer balance adjustments - notes
+
+Nothing could be run here (no PHP or database), so none of this has been executed. Please test it on a copy before relying on it.
+
+## What was added
+
+- **`CustomerAdjustment.php`** adjusts a customer's balance up or down. The fields are direction, amount in the customer's currency, date, reason and GL account. The same page lists the customer's open invoices with a "Write off balance" link, which goes to a confirm form (date, reason, GL account).
+- **`CustomerSmallBalanceWriteOff.php`** is the bulk clean-up. You enter an amount, a date, a reason and a GL account, then the page lists the invoices that qualify. Nothing is posted until you confirm. It is all-or-nothing in one DB transaction.
+- **`includes/CustomerAdjustmentFunctions.php`** holds the shared posting code: `PostCustomerAdjustment()`, `WriteOffCustomerInvoice()` and `CustomerAdjustmentCheckGLAccount()`.
+- **Security:** a new token, **21 "Customer balance adjustments and write-offs"**, is the page security for both pages.
+  - It is granted to the System Administrator role only. Other roles can be given it in Security Roles.
+  - The menu items are only created for role 8, and the link on `SelectCustomer.php` only shows for users holding the token.
+- **Upgrade:** `sql/updates/44.php` creates the token, scripts, the role 8 grant and the menu items. It also makes sure systype 15 exists.
+- **New installs:**
+  - `install/sql/data/{securitytokens,securitygroups,scripts,menuitems}.sql` are updated.
+  - `install/sql/demo.sql` is updated too, because the installer stamps DBUpdateNumber with the highest update file and would otherwise skip 44.
+- **Manual:** a new section in `doc/Manual/ManualARTransactions.html`, plus entries in `ManualSecuritySchema.html` and `ManualOutline.php`.
+
+## How it is posted
+
+- **Transaction type:** the existing type **15 "Journal - Debtors"** is used. It was already in `systypes`, in the translations and in `Z_DeleteSalesTransActions`, but nothing posted it. I did not add a new type.
+- **Debtors record:** the adjustment is a `debtortrans` row of type 15. The amount is in `ovamount`, signed: positive increases the balance, negative decreases it.
+- **GL:** when `gllink_debtors` is on, the entries are debtors control against the chosen account, with the amount converted at the rate. `EnsureGLEntriesBalance` is called.
+- **Numbering and period:** numbers come from `GetNextTransNo(15)`. The period comes from `GetPeriod(date)`, the same as other postings.
+- **Write-off:** it posts a negative type 15 for the full remaining balance and allocates it to the invoice in `custallocns`. Both rows get `alloc` set and `settled=1`, following the sign conventions of `CustomerAllocations.php`.
+
+## Where adjustments now appear
+
+- **Account:** `CustomerAccount.php` has a new row type with debit or credit columns and an allocation link for credits.
+- **Reports and reconciliation:**
+  - `CustomerBalancesMovement.php` counts positive adjustments as debits. Before this, everything that was not an invoice counted as a credit.
+  - `Z_CheckDebtorsControl.php` includes type 15 in the invoices/credits column.
+  - `DebtorsAtPeriodEnd.php` includes type 15 in its exchange-difference clause.
+  - `PDFCustTransListing.php` has a new transaction type.
+- **Matching:**
+  - `CustomerAllocations.php` and `Z_AutoCustomerAllocations.php` accept negative adjustments as sources.
+  - Positive adjustments already show as targets, because the target query takes any unsettled row.
+  - `CustWhereAlloc.php` handles type 15.
+- **Unchanged:** `CustomerInquiry.php`, `PrintCustStatements.php` and `AgedDebtors.php` are generic over type and already showed the new type. The `balance` column is generated, so ageing and balances pick it up automatically.
+
+## Ambiguities and how I resolved them
+
+1. **"Less than an amount we choose"** has no currency.
+   - I used the home currency: the invoice balance divided by the invoice's rate is compared with the amount. The page says so.
+   - A per-customer-currency threshold would be easy to add if preferred.
+2. **"Every customer invoice left open".**
+   - Only type 10 invoices with a positive balance are included.
+   - Unallocated credits and receipts are left alone.
+3. **Exchange rate of an adjustment.**
+   - A manual adjustment uses the customer currency's current rate.
+   - A write-off uses the invoice's own rate, so the debtors control account clears exactly what the invoice put in and there is no exchange difference.
+4. **GL account when the debtors ledger is not linked to the GL.** The account field is not shown and no GL entries are made, since there is nowhere to post them.
+5. **GL account validation.** The control account and bank accounts are refused. The account must also be one the user can update (`glaccountusers.canupd`), as in receipts.
+6. **"Only the people we allow".** I read this as a dedicated security token rather than reusing token 3 (AR clerks).
+   - Existing roles keep their current permissions, so after upgrading only System Administrator has access until you assign token 21 to the roles you want.
+   - Menu entries are only created for role 8. If you assign the token to another role, add the menu items for that role in Menu Items maintenance. The pages and the customer screen link work without them.
+7. **Closed periods.** `GetPeriod()` moves a date in a closed period to the first open one, so I did the same and did not add a stricter check.
+8. **One adjustment per invoice in the bulk run.** This is for auditability. The customer's statement therefore shows one line per written-off invoice.
+9. **Reason storage.** The reason goes in `invtext` and the GL narrative, truncated to 200 characters in the narrative. The `reference` column holds a short label such as "Write off invoice 123".
+10. **Not changed.**
+    - Credit-note/invoice printing is not extended to type 15, as there is no document to print.
+    - The legacy `sql/demo.sql` is not updated.
+    - The API (`api/`) is not extended.
